(4364, 271, 'What is XGBoost known for?', 'Efficient, regularized gradient boosting', 'Simple bagging', 'Linear regression', 'Kernel SVMs', 'A', 'XGBoost is a fast, scalable boosting library.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4365, 271, 'What is stacking?', 'Using a meta-model to combine base model predictions', 'Averaging identical models', 'Deleting models', 'Training one model', 'A', 'Stacking learns how to best combine base predictions.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4366, 271, 'What does the diversity of base models contribute?', 'Different errors that can cancel out', 'Identical outputs', 'Less accuracy', 'No effect', 'A', 'Diversity makes ensembles more robust.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4367, 271, 'Which sampling does bagging use?', 'Bootstrap sampling with replacement', 'Stratified fixed sampling', 'No sampling', 'Sequential sampling', 'A', 'Bootstrap samples vary the training data per model.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4368, 271, 'What is hard voting?', 'Majority vote of class predictions', 'Averaging probabilities', 'Weighted regression', 'Deleting votes', 'A', 'Hard voting chooses the most common class.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4369, 271, 'What is soft voting?', 'Averaging predicted probabilities', 'Counting classes', 'Choosing one model', 'Deleting models', 'A', 'Soft voting averages class probabilities.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4370, 271, 'Why are random forests less prone to overfitting than single trees?', 'Averaging many decorrelated trees reduces variance', 'They ignore data', 'They use one tree', 'They delete features', 'A', 'Averaging smooths individual tree errors.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(4371, 271, 'What is the key difference between bagging and boosting?', 'Bagging trains in parallel on samples; boosting trains sequentially on errors', 'They are identical', 'Bagging boosts weights', 'Boosting averages samples', 'A', 'Bagging reduces variance; boosting reduces bias.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4372, 271, 'What is the role of learning rate in boosting?', 'Shrinking each model''s contribution to avoid overfitting', 'Speeding data loading', 'Setting cluster count', 'Choosing features', 'A', 'Smaller learning rates require more trees but generalize better.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4373, 271, 'What does AdaBoost''s weight update emphasize?', 'Misclassified examples get higher weights', 'Correct examples get higher weights', 'All weights stay equal', 'Weights are deleted', 'A', 'Harder examples drive subsequent learners.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4374, 271, 'What is a limitation of AdaBoost with noisy data?', 'It can overemphasize outliers and overfit', 'It ignores outliers', 'It always generalizes', 'It needs no learners', 'A', 'Noise can misdirect AdaBoost''s weighting.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4375, 271, 'What is the purpose of feature subsampling in random forests?', 'Decorrelating trees by using random feature subsets', 'Deleting features', 'Adding features', 'Labeling data', 'A', 'Feature randomness reduces correlation among trees.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4376, 271, 'Which boosting algorithm uses second-order gradients?', 'XGBoost', 'AdaBoost', 'Random forest', 'Simple bagging', 'A', 'XGBoost uses first and second derivatives for optimization.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4377, 271, 'What is the benefit of gradient boosting over random forest on some tasks?', 'It often achieves higher accuracy by correcting residuals', 'It is always simpler', 'It needs no tuning', 'It ignores features', 'A', 'Sequential residual fitting can yield better accuracy.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4378, 271, 'What is a meta-model in stacking?', 'The model that learns to combine base predictions', 'A single base tree', 'The dataset', 'The label set', 'A', 'The meta-model blends base learner outputs.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4379, 271, 'What is the main risk of overfitting in boosting?', 'Too many boosting rounds can memorize noise', 'More trees reduce accuracy always', 'Boosting cannot overfit', 'No risk exists', 'A', 'Excessive rounds lead to overfitting.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(4380, 271, 'How does early stopping help boosted trees?', 'It halts training when validation performance stops improving', 'It deletes trees', 'It adds noise', 'It slows training', 'A', 'Early stopping controls boosting rounds.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
